    "reward_lens.studies.freeze.freeze": {
      "path": "reward_lens.studies.freeze.freeze",
      "name": "freeze",
      "kind": "function",
      "text": "Freeze a study spec, computing its StudyID and recording the git sha (gate 3).\n\nThe StudyID is ``study:{spec.id}@v{spec.version}#{hash8}`` where the hash is the first 8 hex\ncharacters of the spec's content hash. Two specs that differ in any registered field (a\nprediction threshold, a kill criterion, the analysis path) get different ids, which is exactly\nthe property that makes post-hoc editing visible as a new version.",
      "params": [],
      "returns": [],
      "raises": [],
      "examples": [],
      "admonitions": [],
      "source": {
